 "_about": "RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-25 (rd/plus-ones-are-rows: the owner’s “Each plus shouldn’t come from a drop down…”, “one at a time”, “Tick only shows when there is name written. and that is required. If you are not yet sure, delete name” and “Yes, build the +1 screens as shown.” — each +1 is its own screen (its own step, “+N · Not sure yet? Leave the name empty.”), the “Filling in for” picker gone; a named +1 gets the required “They’re coming” tick (the house tick, shared with the Terms line, whose box now fills with the page’s paper instead of white); meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-25 (rd/rsvp-seats-first: the owner’s approved RSVP seats-first prototype, “all as recommended” — after “Joyfully accepts” the card says the seats first (“We reserved N seats for you”, tiles You · +1 · +2, one line + ⓘ), then the You step (the name read-only with “Wrong name? Tell the couple”, then “What should we call you?” and Mobile — the contact boxes moved up from the end), then the +1 names (its line now names the seats, the count line and the summary line gone), then the tagging question, then the rest; a No keeps its contact step after the note, posted as `declined_contact_*`; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-24 (rd/held-pass-reply-identity: the card’s default question reads “Will you join us?” — the Event Hub Reply card’s own words, “event” never “celebration” — in place of “Will you celebrate with us?”; a couple’s own question is unchanged; meant for every guest whose couple typed none). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-21 (rd/every-hub-button-works: the guest-to-host line under the card is a 44 px press, `min-h-[40px]` → `min-h-[44px]` in guest-to-host-cta.tsx — the Hub button walk; only the three “a host pitch” cases move, same byte length; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 2 again, batch-4 walk: the terms line is a wrapping flex row whose links are 44px boxes of their own — no two press zones overlap when “Privacy Notice” wraps; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 2: the terms line’s two links are positioned above the sentence text and “Privacy Notice” does not break — meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (rd/hub-leftovers item 1: every later step’s question — tagging, plus-ones, meal, dietary, song, note, contact — wears step 1’s 32 px question line, one-at-a-time cards only; meant for every guest). Before that RECORDED AGAIN 2026-10-13 (release batch 3 joining main: #6488 guest-leftovers-2 — the Terms line one shared piece and faint ink /45–/60 → /70, meant for every guest — together with main’s rd/reply-steps-one-look below; both sides had re-recorded, the join is recorded once). Before that 2026-10-13 (rd/reply-steps-one-look: the tagging question’s answers wear the card’s own answer — the style’s one class, the Look › Buttons hook and, on the reply card, the couple’s Yes / No look — meant for every guest asked it; only the three “the tagging question asked” cases move). Before that 2026-10-12 (rd/release-leftovers: the terms line’s two links pressable at 44px, its “Required” readable at 4.5:1 — meant for every guest). First recorded 2026-10-10 from RsvpWidget AS IT STOOD at origin/main 64746f064, BEFORE the reply card’s lines were drawn from a list (the RSVP stage’s ＋, drag and Group). Each case is the sha-256 and the byte length of the whole card’s HTML (react-dom/server renderToStaticMarkup); `inFull` keeps the reply’s own fieldset of two cases so a person can read it. `widgetSha256` is rsvp-widget.tsx at recording — compare with `git show 64746f064:\"apps/web/app/[slug]/_components/rsvp-widget.tsx\" | shasum -a 256`. Held by the-reply-card-is-todays-page.test.ts. Record again ONLY when the card is meant to change for every guest.",
